# Korber2026_GLIMPSE_z7p5
# Paper: Korber et al. 2026, A&A 708, A43 (GLIMPSE, Abell S1063), doi:10.1051/0004-6361/202556868;
#   arXiv:2510.04771 (v2 = A&A proof-corrected version, checked)
# Source: Appendix C, Table C.4 ("[OIII]5008 LF", label tab:O35007LF), <z> ~ 7.48 block.
# Redshift: 7 < z < 8 (photometric, F090W-dropout Lyman-break sample); mean z = 7.48 -> file labelled z = 7.5
# Line: [O III] lambda5008. CAVEAT: this is NOT a direct line measurement. The paper measures the combined
#   Hbeta+[OIII]4960,5008 luminosity from SED fitting (CIGALE) of broad/medium-band photometry (Table C.1 is that
#   primary Hbeta+[OIII] LF, NOT used here), then splits off [OIII]5008 with an assumed M_UV-dependent R3 =
#   [OIII]5008/Hbeta relation (their Eq. for R3(M_UV), R3 = 1.49-6.34). The [OIII]5008 LF is therefore model dependent.
# Luminosities are de-lensed (intrinsic); effective volumes include lensing. Bins of 0.5 dex (centres listed).
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3
# Errors: symmetric 1-sigma in dex (mean +- std over SED/magnification/completeness realisations; Poisson and
#   volume/completeness errors combined). The faintest bins have very low completeness (<C> ~ 0.13-0.25)
#   and S/N < 2 at logL = 38.25 and 42.25 (S/N and <C> from the table given as trailing comments).
#
# Columns:
# Log10(L_[OIII]5008 / erg s^-1)
# Log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 dex^-1)
# 1-sigma delta in dex (symmetric)
#
38.25  -0.33  0.62   # N=4.33  <C>=0.13  S/N=1.45
38.75  -0.48  0.35   # N=9.87  <C>=0.19  S/N=2.76
